__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/*.sqlite3
.venv/
runs/
.DS_Store
downloads/

# Benchmark geometry is NOT redistributed (workshop terms), but its record is.
# Gap J5: with the whole directory ignored, the KCS "-0.09% on displacement"
# validation silently skipped on every machine but the one that generated the
# file, and nothing in the repo said what the missing file should have been.
# The pattern must be `dir/*`, not `dir/`: git will not re-include a path
# inside a directory it has already excluded.
data/benchmark_geom/*
!data/benchmark_geom/CHECKSUMS.json

# BUILD ARTIFACTS, gap J6. `data/exports/hull.{iges,step}` are REGENERATED by
# the test suite on every run, so tracking them dirtied the tree constantly —
# they were re-modified by 5 of the last 10 commits, caused cherry-pick
# conflicts, and provoked an unasked `git checkout --` by another agent.
# `renders/` held 9 committed PNGs (~2.3 MB) of CFD output that is reproducible
# from the runs.
data/exports/
renders/

badFaces
illegalFaces
selfInterPoints.obj
*.obj

# The evolution spine keeps a machine-local, append-only history:
#   data/evolution/archive.jsonl  every genome, every state change
#   data/evolution/gaps.jsonl     the live gap queue
# Gitignored for the same reason as data/exports/ and renders/ (gap J6): a
# file the test suite rewrites on every run dirties the tree constantly and
# conflicts on every cherry-pick. It is one machine's own history, not a
# shared artefact -- the record that must survive is docs/GAP-REGISTER.md.
#
# TRACKING gaps.jsonl WAS PROPOSED 2026-08-07 AND REJECTED, deliberately. The
# finding was real -- a fresh clone has no queue and none of the 83 recorded
# closures -- but the file is the wrong fix for it:
#   - the log is DERIVED. Every closure in it was written by --apply from a
#     predicate over code that is already tracked, so committing it stores a
#     conclusion beside its own evidence (a number declared twice, this
#     codebase's recurring defect) and the log is the copy that goes stale.
#   - it cannot be merged. It is append-only, four records per closure, and
#     GapQueue.next_id mints ids by scanning the log it has: two agents closing
#     two different gaps both mint G-120 and NEITHER side of the merge is
#     right. data/exports/* taught the cheap version of this lesson already.
# What the decision owes instead is reconstructibility and noise, and both are
# now enforced by tests/test_reconcile_gaps.py:
#     python scripts/reconcile_gaps.py --rebuild     # register + predicates
# and an absent queue exits non-zero with a banner rather than reporting an
# empty register as if there were nothing to do.
data/evolution/

# Agent worktrees are scratch checkouts, never content.
.claude/worktrees/

# `scripts/blender_compare.py` writes one STL per arm per hull here: 8 arms x
# 3 hulls is ~1.5 GB, and the largest single file measured is a 232 MB ascii
# STL (the subsurf-1-finecage arm, 1155588 triangles). They are REGENERATED by
# re-running the script and none of them is evidence -- the numbers live in
# docs/research/BLENDER.md. Tracking them would dirty the tree on every run,
# which data/exports/* already taught this repository once.
data/blender/

# Gap J6, SECOND OCCURRENCE. `docs/research/*.png` held 2.7 MB of hull-facet
# renders that are reproducible from `stl_forensics.render_facets` — the same
# defect the `renders/` rule above already records, in a directory that rule
# did not cover.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-12, and it is why this is not merely about repository size:
# stl-hull04/08/14.png were rendered at 14:53 and committed at 15:41, while
# `bbf1a47` (the chine row) landed at 15:22 BETWEEN them. The committed images
# were therefore pictures of a surface the code had already stopped producing,
# in a document that cites them as evidence. A binary artifact cannot carry a
# diff, so nothing could have shown that it had gone stale.
#
# docs/research/STL.md carries the command that regenerates them from the
# CURRENT geometry.
docs/research/*.png

# THE README HERO IMAGE IS AN ASSET, NOT A BUILD ARTIFACT, and the distinction
# is the whole of gap J6 rather than an exception to it.
#
# `renders/` and `docs/research/*.png` are ignored because they held PNGs that
# are REPRODUCIBLE from a script and therefore go stale silently: the three
# hull renders committed on 2026-08-12 were rendered at 14:53 and committed at
# 15:41, while the chine fix landed at 15:22 BETWEEN them, so they were
# pictures of a surface the code had already stopped producing. A binary
# artifact cannot carry a diff, so nothing could have shown that.
#
# `docs/assets/` is different in the one way that matters: nothing regenerates
# it. It is authored once, it depicts no measured state, and it cannot fall out
# of step with the code because it makes no claim about the code. It must be
# tracked or README.md renders a broken image on GitHub.
#
# The test is not "is it a PNG", it is "could this silently disagree with the
# code". Put a rendered result here and the rule has been broken, not widened.
!docs/assets/
skips.log
# Captured suite logs. A PATTERN, not a hand-kept list:
# this was five literal filenames and grew by one every
# session that ran the suite -- the hand-maintained copy
# defect, applied to ignore rules. A log worth KEEPING
# goes to docs/audit/ with a date in its name.
full-suite*.log
# DSYHS source spreadsheets: re-downloadable from 4TU with published MD5s
# (see benchmarks/dsyhs.py). The EXTRACTED dsyhs_modelscale.json is tracked.
data/refdata/dsyhs/*.xlsx
# The DSYHS geometry release (16 MB of IGES). Restored by
# scripts/fetch_e5_geometry.py against the PUBLISHER'S OWN MD5. What gets
# committed is the extracted offsets under tests/e5_real_hulls/, which a
# naval architect can read and a reviewer can diff.
data/refdata/dsyhs/*.zip

# Kit-lane BUILD ARTIFACTS. Same rule as data/exports/ and renders/ one line
# up: an STL and a nested DXF are REGENERATED by the lane that produced them,
# so tracking them dirties the tree on every run and conflicts on every
# cherry-pick. The campaign JSON beside them is NOT an artifact — it is the
# measurement, and it is tracked exactly as data/gate2u-16gene-solve.json is.
data/campaigns/kit/

# The provenance DB is REGENERABLE, not evidence. Its L3 rows come from
# `scripts/ingest_cfd_campaign.py` over runs/ + the tracked campaign JSON, and
# its L1 rows from `evaluate` over the same population — so tracking it would
# be a second copy of numbers that already have a home, and a binary one that
# conflicts on every write. The EVIDENCE is data/campaigns/*.json and the force
# histories; the DB is the index built over them.
data/provenance.db
data/provenance.db-journal

# Regenerable from scripts/build_plywood_catamaran_corpus.py (parameters + seed).
# 5 MB of derived labels; summary.json carries the measured rates.
data/plywood_catamaran/labels.csv
data/plywood_catamaran/stls/

# 36 MB of per-hull descriptor rows, regenerable by
# scripts/build_shipd_corpus.py --seed 0. The BANDS are committed.
data/shipd_morphology.json
downloads/shipd/
